The original project provides the Android system cursor, Shizuku virtual-mouse
architecture and external-display touchpad foundation. This fork adds and
reworks fullscreen controls, Pocket mode, external settings, orientation
calibration, input preferences, testing and reliability improvements.

The fork's source packages, AIDL interface, JNI bindings and Android namespace
have been migrated to au.com.michaelcarey.artouchpad. This identifies the
independently maintained fork and does not replace credit for the original work.

